+The `return` statement is a non-standard extension to Go's [`text/template`][] package. It terminates execution of the current template. Used within _partial_ templates, it also returns the given value, if any.
 
 The returned value may be of any data type including, but not limited to, [`bool`](g), [`float`](g), [`int`](g), [`map`](g), [`resource`](g), [`slice`](g), or [`string`](g).
 
